{"id":"12G","title":"Drinking and Drunkenness","part":{"n":12,"title":"Etiquette and moral issues"},"url":"/law/12-etiquette-and-moral-issues/12g","entries":[{"id":"12G.1","text":"Sobriety commanded.","refs":[{"book":"1 Thessalonians","chapter":5,"verses":"6,8"},{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":1,"verses":"13"},{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":4,"verses":"7"},{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":5,"verses":"8"}],"citation":"1 Thes. 5:6, 8; 1 Pet. 1: 13; 1 Pet. 4:7; 1 Pet. 5:8."},{"id":"12G.2","text":"The gospel teaches we should live soberly.","refs":[{"book":"Titus","chapter":2,"verses":"12"}],"citation":"Titus 2:12."},{"id":"12G.3","text":"The taking of wine or strong drink is forbidden when going into the tabernacle of the congregation.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":10,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Lev. 10:9."},{"id":"12G.4","text":"Those in the service of God are not to drink alcohol.","refs":[{"book":"Numbers","chapter":6,"verses":"2-3"}],"citation":"Num. 6:2-3."},{"id":"12G.5","text":"Drinking and Drunkenness not approved.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":21,"verses":"20"},{"book":"Hosea","chapter":4,"verses":"11"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":21,"verses":"34"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":13,"verses":"13"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":14,"verses":"21"},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":6,"verses":"10"},{"book":"Galatians","chapter":5,"verses":"21"},{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":5,"verses":"18"}],"citation":"Deut. 21:20; Hosea 4:11; Luke 21:34; Rom. 13:13; Rom. 14:21; 1 Cor. 6:10; Gal. 5:21; Eph. 5:18."},{"id":"12G.6","text":"Drinking and merrymaking prevents the people from seeing the afflictions of the nation.","refs":[{"book":"Joel","chapter":1,"verses":"4-7"},{"book":"Amos","chapter":6,"verses":"1-7"}],"citation":"Joel 1:4-7; Amos 6:1-7."},{"id":"12G.7","text":"Excessive or habitual drinking is admonished against, as it causes a disregard of the judgments and works of God.","refs":[{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":5,"verses":"11-12"}],"citation":"Isa. 5:11-12."},{"id":"12G.8","text":"Pregnant women are not to take alcoholic drinks.","refs":[{"book":"Judges","chapter":13,"verses":"3-4,79"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":1,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"Judges 13:3-4, 79 14; Luke 1:15."},{"id":"12G.9","text":"Intoxicating drink causes persons to err and be led astray.","refs":[{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":28,"verses":"7"}],"citation":"Isa. 28:7."},{"id":"12G.10","text":"We are not to associate with those that are drunkards and gluttons.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":23,"verses":"20"},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":5,"verses":"11"}],"citation":"Prov. 23:20; 1 Cor. 5:11."},{"id":"12G.11","text":"Addiction to intoxicating drink brings sorrow, contentions, complaints, wounds without cause, and redness of eyes.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":23,"verses":"29-35"}],"citation":"Prov. 23:29-35."},{"id":"12G.12","text":"Wine is a mocker, strong drink arouses brawling, and whoever is intoxicated by it is deluded and not wise.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":20,"verses":"1"}],"citation":"Prov. 20:1."},{"id":"12G.13","text":"You are not to encourage another to drink or attempt to get another drunk.","refs":[{"book":"Habakkuk","chapter":2,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"Hab. 2:15."}]}